course: dictionary
lesson: 9210
title: Solemnly: serious and formal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how something is done. Solemnly is an adverb, so it describes an action. It means in a very serious way, without smiling or joking.
explain: «Then the Dodo solemnly presents her own thimble back to Alice» tells us the Dodo is serious about it, not joking. The clues around the word help: the Dodo is giving a prize, and Alice keeps a straight face, which shows the moment is supposed to be taken seriously.
explain: Solemnly can also mean in a formal, important way, as in a promise or ceremony. «I solemnly swear» is said before a vow, so the listeners know it matters. Try swapping in a word like seriously: if it fits, you are probably on the right track.
fact: Solemnly is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Solemnly» means in a very serious way, without smiling or joking.
fact: «Solemnly» can also mean in a formal, important way, like a promise or ceremony.
fact: «Solemnly» often comes up at funerals, church services, prize-givings and oaths.
fact: In old English, «grave» means serious, and «solemnly» means very seriously.
exercise: «The Dodo solemnly presents her own thimble to Alice.» What does solemnly mean? | In a sleepy way | In a loud, rushing way | In a silly, giggly way | *In a very serious way, without smiling or joking
exercise: «I solemnly swear» is said before a promise. What does solemnly suggest? | In a funny way | *In a formal, important way | In a whispered, secret way | In a quick, careless way
exercise: «Grave» is an old word for serious. Which word means the same as «solemnly» in this old sense? | happily | *very seriously | quickly | quietly
test: Which sentence uses solemnly in the formal sense? | The dog solemnly chased its ball | We solemnly laughed at the joke | The clown solemnly threw a pie at the crowd | *The mayor solemnly lit the candle at the ceremony
test: In Alice, creatures speak solemnly about silly things. Why does this make readers laugh? | The words are silly | Solemn means happy | Nobody can read the words | *Serious manners clash with silly things
exam: Which word means in a very serious way, without smiling or joking? | Gently | Happily | *Solemnly | Quickly
